At a collapsing level there are a projective $\mathbb Q$-factorial Fano type model $Y$ of $K$, a contraction $\pi:Y\to V$ with $\dim V<\dim S$, an effective ample rational Cartier divisor $H_V$ on $V$, and a rational $x\asymp s^{-1}$ with the following properties. The pivot survives on $Y$, and it is the only horizontal prime in the positive support of the trace $H''$ of $H$. Moreover $$x=\frac{b_*}{H_*},\qquad H_*\asymp s,
 \qquad xH''-J''=x\pi^*H_V,$$ with $J$ as just defined. On common higher models, $$\label{eq:B4}
                          H\ge\pi^*H_V.$$ The datum with b-nef part $\mathbf M_C=\mathbf M'+(x-d')\overline H$ and boundary obtained by subtracting $J$ from the $A'$-boundary has effective uniformly generalized positive-lc trace on $Y$, with total adjoint $x\pi^*H_V$. The geometric generic fibres of $\pi$ form a bounded family.

At the final level one may take $Y=S$ up to a small $\mathbb Q$-factorialization, with target a point, and choose a fixed small rational $x>0$ so that $$C=A'+xH=a_K+\mathbf M_C,
 \qquad \mathbf M_C=\mathbf M'+(x-d')\overline H$$ is effective and uniformly generalized klt. Its b-nef big part has a fixed positive $H$-reserve, its boundary dominates a fixed positive multiple of $H$, and the underlying $Y$ belongs to a bounded family. For every invariant prime with restriction $E|_{k(S)}=cP\ne0$, $$\label{b:scale-terminal-bound}
                         cC(P)\le1-\frac{h_E}{2}.$$

For every effective rational $\mathbb Q$-Cartier divisor $L'$ on $\mathcal F_i$ and every horizontal test $P$, $$\label{eq:C1}
              P(L')\le C_0\deg(L')C_i(P).$$ If $\mathbf U$ is rational b-Cartier and b-nef, with trace $U_{\rm tr}$ on $Y_i$, then $$\label{eq:C2}
 0\le P(\overline{U_{\rm tr}}-\mathbf U)
                  \le C_0\deg(U_{\rm tr})C_i(P).$$

For $D_1\ge0$, $D_1\sim_\mathbb QH_1$ on $S_1$, and every divisorial test $P_1$, with restriction multiplicities included in $P_i=P_1|_{K_i}$, one has $$\label{eq:C3}
                         D_1(P_1)\le C_0\sum_i a_i(P_i).$$ For tests trivial on $K_f$, this implies $$\label{eq:C4}
 D_1(P_1)\le C_0\bigl(H_1(P_1)+s_{\exp}A_1^+(P_1)\bigr),
 \qquad s_{\exp}:=\max_{i<f}s_i\longrightarrow0,$$ where an empty maximum is zero.

If $\beta\in M_0$, $\|\beta\|\le L$, and $L\ge1$, then there are $m\in n\mathbb Z_{\ge0}$ and a bounded positive integer $d_0$, with $m\lesssim L$, such that $$\label{eq:C5}
                R_{m\chi+d_0\beta}\ne0,\qquad
                R_{m\chi-d_0\beta}\ne0 .$$

For every occurring weight $\mu=m\chi+\beta$ of positive cost $B'=\widetilde v(\mu)$, $$\label{eq:C7}
                     \dim R_\mu\lesssim
                           \prod_i(1+B's_i)^{p_i}.$$ At each fixed physical degree $m$, the dimension through cost $S'\ge0$, including constants if present, is at most $$\label{eq:C8}
                           C_3\prod_j(1+S'/W_j).$$ For $m\in n\mathbb Z_{\ge0}$, the same expression bounds the truncated associated graded dimension of $V_m$.

For the invariant valuation $Q$ of Lemma <a href="#c:invariantization" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="c:invariantization">51</a>, there are real monomial valuations $w_\lambda$, for small $\lambda>0$, such that $$\label{eq:E2}
 \begin{split}
 w_\lambda(F)&=w(F)+\lambda Q(\overline F),\\
 A_\theta(w_\lambda)&=A_\theta(w)+\lambda A_{\theta_w}(Q).
 \end{split}$$ For each fixed nonzero rational function the first identity holds for all sufficiently small $\lambda$, with the interval allowed to depend on that function. If $w$ is Gaussian on a prescribed finite list $y$, and $Q$ is Gaussian on $\overline y$, then $w_\lambda$ may be kept Gaussian on $y$.

For every nontrivial real Abhyankar valuation $Q^\dagger$ of $L/k'$, $$\label{eq:E4}
 A_{\theta_{w,\mathrm{rel}}}(Q^\dagger)
       \ge \kappa\min_{i\ \mathrm{active}}
                       \frac{Q^\dagger(\overline F_i)}{b_i}.$$ An active cap contributes the entry zero. If equality holds, then $Q^\dagger(\overline F)<0$ for some actual angular function $F$.

Let $L$ be a finitely generated field over an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic zero, let $\vartheta=
u/f^{1/n}$ be a fractional rational volume form, and let $I\subset L^*$ be a nonempty finite system whose ratios generate $L/k$. Let $k_I$ be a positive integer. Suppose that every prime divisor $P$ over a proper model of $L/k$ satisfies $$\label{eq:E6}
 A_\vartheta(P)> rac{\min P(I)}{k_I}.$$ After spreading these data, in sufficiently general reductions of arbitrarily large characteristic $\mathfrak p\equiv1\pmod{nk_I}$ there are $l\ge1$ and $H\in\operatorname{span}(I^{(P_0-1)/k_I})$, where $P_0=\mathfrak p^l$, such that $$\label{eq:E7}
 \mathcal C^l_\vartheta(H)
 := rac{\mathcal C^l igl(Hf^{(P_0-1)/n}
u igr)}{
u}
e0.$$ Here $\mathcal C^l$ is iterated Cartier trace on rational top forms over perfect constants. One may choose $H$ to be a single product from $I^{(P_0-1)/k_I}$.

Transport $w$ to a reduction of its monomial chart, using the same positive normal weights. Let $x$ consist of its normal parameters and a unit separating tangential basis. Retain the conditions that $x$ is a $\mathfrak p$-basis of the actual field and that its initials form a $\mathfrak p$-basis of $K_w$. Write $$\theta=\frac{\bigwedge_jd\log x_j}{f_x^{1/n}}.$$ For $\mathfrak p\equiv1\pmod n$, $P_0=\mathfrak p^l$, and every $G$ in the reduced actual field, $$\label{eq:E8}
 w\bigl(\mathcal C^l_\theta(G)\bigr)
 \ge \frac{w(G)}{P_0}
      -\left(1-\frac1{P_0}\right)A_\theta(w).$$ We set $w(0)=+\infty$. For $G\ne0$, equality holds if and only if $\mathcal C^l_{\theta_w}(\bar G)\ne0$; in that case $$\overline{\mathcal C^l_\theta(G)}
       =\mathcal C^l_{\theta_w}(\bar G).$$ The discrepancy in <a href="#eq:E8" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:E8">[eq:E8]</a> is the characteristic-zero numerical quantity transported by the chart formula. The same assertions hold with ordered monomial weights, and the inequality holds under local real weight variation within the same open stratum cone.

Fix $r\ge1$ and $A>0$. There are constants $N_0,D_0,C_0$, depending only on $r,A$, with the following property. Let $T\ge1$, let $t_1,\ldots,t_r$ be linearly independent over $\mathbb Q$, and let $s\in\mathbb R$. For an integer $N\ge N_0$, set $L=\lceil NT\rceil$. Suppose that $$\#\{as+\alpha\cdot t:0\le a<N,\quad
                    \alpha\in\{0,\ldots,L-1\}^r\}
       \le A(NT)^r.$$ Then $s=\gamma\cdot t$ for a unique $\gamma\in\mathbb Q^r$. The order of $\gamma$ in $\mathbb Q^r/\mathbb Z^r$ is at most $D_0$, and $|\gamma|\le C_0T$.

Fix the constant $B_0$ of Proposition <a href="#c:cheap-collapse" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="c:cheap-collapse">64</a> and a positive constant $c$. For each sufficiently small fixed $\delta>0$, consider any actual monomial valuation $w$, Gaussian on $y$, such that $w(y)=0$, $A_\theta(w)\le1$, and $$\label{eq:F3}
               w(F)+\delta B_0m\ge c\delta b(F)
               \qquad(0\ne F\in V_m).$$ For all sufficiently late sequence members, uniformly over all these valuations and angular functions, $$\label{eq:F4}
                        |w(F)|\le C_6\delta b(F).$$ The constant $C_6$ is independent of the small fixed $\delta$; the index after which the assertion holds may depend on $\delta$.

For every fixed $J\ge1$, on sufficiently late members, $$\label{eq:G2}
                   \dim E_J\asymp
                      J^s\prod_{j\le s}\frac{S}{W_j}.$$ The comparison constants are independent of $J$ and $\delta$; the required lateness may depend on both.

For every absolute tolerance $\sigma>0$, a rank increase followed by a bounded integral scaling and rounding of the new parameters changes a small objective bound according to $$\label{eq:G4}
 e_{\mathrm{new}}=K(\sigma,d)e_{\mathrm{old}}
                                    +C_{10}\sigma.$$ Old parameters remain integral and cheap parameters remain zero. The constants for probe and parameter sizes remain uniform at every later fixed scaling.
